      "id": "ch03_q03",
      "answer": "a. Expanding $(x_i-\\bar{x})^2$ and using $\\sum x_i=n\\bar{x}$ gives $\\sum(x_i-\\bar{x})^2=\\sum x_i^2-2\\bar{x}\\sum x_i+n\\bar{x}^2=\\sum x_i^2-n\\bar{x}^2$.\n\nb. $n=6$, $\\sum x_i=807$, and $\\sum x_i^2=109925$. Thus $\\bar{x}=807/6=134.5$ and\n\n$$s^2=\\frac{109925-6(134.5)^2}{5}=276.7,\\qquad s=\\sqrt{276.7}\\approx16.634.$$\n\nThe deviation formula gives the same $s^2$ because $\\sum(x_i-134.5)^2=1383.5$ and $1383.5/5=276.7$.\n\nc. The intervals are [117.866, 151.134] dollars, [101.232, 167.768] dollars, and [84.598, 184.402] dollars for one, two, and three standard deviations.\n\nd. Yes. $190>184.402$, so it is more than three sample standard deviations above the mean and is unusually high under the normal model.",
      "review_status": "independently solved and reviewed",
      "audit_pack": "ch03-review-v1",
