      "id": "ch03_q30",
      "answer": "a.\n\n| $x$ | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| $p(x)$ | $1/15$ | $2/15$ | $3/15$ | $4/15$ | $5/15$ |\n\nb. Every probability is nonnegative and $\\sum p(x)=(1+2+3+4+5)/15=1$.\n\nc.\n\n$$\\mu_X=\\sum xp(x)=\\frac{55}{15}=\\frac{11}{3}\\approx3.667,$$\n\n$$E(X^{2})=\\frac{1^{3}+2^{3}+3^{3}+4^{3}+5^{3}}{15}=15,$$\n\n$$\\sigma_X^{2}=15-\\left(\\frac{11}{3}\\right)^{2}=\\frac{14}{9}\\approx1.556,$$\n\n$$\\sigma_X=\\sqrt{14}/3\\approx1.247.$$",
