      "answer": "Under the claim, $X\\sim\\operatorname{Binomial}(250,0.05)$, with $\\mu=np=12.5$ and $\\sigma=\\sqrt{np(1-p)}=\\sqrt{11.875}\\approx3.446$. With continuity correction,\n\n$$z=\\frac{39.5-12.5}{3.446}\\approx7.84,$$\n\nso $P(X\\ge40)\\approx P(Z\\ge7.84)\\approx0$. Observing 40 or more is extraordinarily unlikely if $p=0.05$, so the data provide strong evidence against the company's claim.",
